    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\n### Issue Description\r\n\r\nI want to use `C-j` and `C-k` to move up and down in the selection and file preview in `minipick`. I’ve tried configuring it but haven’t been successful. Is there a way to bind these keys for this functionality?\r\n\r\n\r\n### What I’ve Tried\r\n\r\n- Modified key mappings in the config, but it didn’t work.\r\n- Searched the documentation and issues, but couldn’t find a solution.\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\n- `C-j` should move the selection down.\r\n- `C-k` should move the selection up.\r\n\r\nThanks for your help!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Issue Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I want to use <code class=\"notranslate\">C-j</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">C-k</code> to move up and down in the selection and file preview in <code class=\"notranslate\">minipick</code>. I’ve tried configuring it but haven’t been successful. Is there a way to bind these keys for this functionality?</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What I’ve Tried</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Modified key mappings in the config, but it didn’t work.</li>\n<li>Searched the documentation and issues, but couldn’t find a solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected Behavior</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">C-j</code> should move the selection down.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">C-k</code> should move the selection up.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for your help!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nIssue Description\nI want to use C-j and C-k to move up and down in the selection and file preview in minipick. I’ve tried configuring it but haven’t been successful. Is there a way to bind these keys for this functionality?\nWhat I’ve Tried\n\nModified key mappings in the config, but it didn’t work.\nSearched the documentation and issues, but couldn’t find a solution.\n\nExpected Behavior\n\nC-j should move the selection down.\nC-k should move the selection up.\n\nThanks for your help!",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
